  "tagline": "Sybase's pioneering columnar warehouse, now SAP IQ and the engine behind HANA Cloud's data lake.",
  "description": "SAP IQ, formerly Sybase IQ, was one of the first commercial column-store databases, shipping in the mid-1990s with bitmap-style indexes and heavy compression for read-mostly analytics. Its multiplex architecture lets several nodes share the same storage for scale-out reads and loads. SAP now positions it mainly as a cost-efficient warm store next to SAP HANA, as the data lake relational engine in SAP HANA Cloud, and for near-line storage in SAP BW. It is stable and proven but legacy: new non-SAP analytics projects almost never start on it.",
